  "steps": [
    "Boil 60g raw soya chunks in hot water with 1 tsp salt until softened. Squeeze out all the excess water.",
    "Transfer the soya chunks to a bowl and add: 1 tsp black pepper powder, 1 tsp red chilli powder, 1 tsp ginger garlic paste, Mix everything really well. Now add 2 tbsp cornstarch and toss until the soya chunks are evenly coated.",
    "Pop them into an air fryer at 200°C for 10 minutes, flipping halfway through.",
    "Once they’re lightly golden and crispy, take them out and set aside.",
    "Now let’s make the sauce!",
    "In a bowl, add: 1 tbsp Schezwan sauce, 2 tbsp soy sauce, ¼ cup green chilli sauce, ½ cup tomato ketchup, 1 tsp vinegar, ½ tsp salt, ½ tsp cornstarch, 50ml water, Mix everything really well until combined.",
    "Now heat 1 tbsp oil in a pan on medium heat. Add 8 finely chopped garlic cloves and 10g ginger. Sauté until fragrant. Then add 1 finely chopped onion and sauté until lightly golden.",
    "Now toss in: 1 chopped green chilli, ½ diced onion, ½ diced bell pepper.",
    "Turn up the heat and sauté until the veggies lose their raw bite but still have a nice crunch.",
    "Now add the crispy soya chunks and pour in the prepared sauce.",
    "Toss everything together and cook on high heat for 2 minutes until the sauce coats the soya chunks beautifully.",
    "Finish with ½ handful of fresh coriander, give it one final toss, and it’s ready to serve!"
  ],
